<h2>What happens when the site starts</h2>
<ol class="docs-steps">
    <li>Configuration is loaded from <code>appsettings.json</code>, <code>appsettings.{Environment}.json</code> (not in Production) and environment variables.</li>
    <li>The app connects to Key Vault using <code>EnvironmentCredential</code> (the <code>KEY_VAULT_URL</code>, <code>AZURE_TENANT_ID</code>, <code>AZURE_CLIENT_ID</code> and <code>AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET</code> environment variables). If this fails, the app can't start.</li>
    <li>It reads the database connection string (<code>db-connection-live</code> in Production; <code>ConnectionStrings:Development</code> in Development) and sets up Serilog (Loki + <code>applicationlogs</code>).</li>
    <li>Identity, permission policies, password rules, Data Protection (keys in blob storage, wrapped by Key Vault), cookies, HSTS, ELMAH, Hangfire (MySQL storage), SignalR, blob services and the optional ChurchSuite OAuth handler are registered.</li>
    <li>Pending EF Core migrations are applied automatically.</li>
    <li>The seeder makes sure every permission and the three built-in roles exist with the right permissions, creates the first SuperAdmin from <code>sys-admin-username</code> / <code>sys-admin-password</code> if missing (with a <em>Default Church</em> listing), and makes sure the <code>bulletins</code> table exists.</li>
    <li>Hosted services start: the Hangfire server, <code>LogWatcherService</code>, and <code>ImageMigrationHostedService</code> (does nothing unless <code>ImageMigration:Enabled</code> is true).</li>
</ol>

<h2>How a request flows through the web app</h2>
<p>Each request passes through this middleware, in order:</p>
<ol class="docs-steps">
    <li><strong>Exception handler and HSTS</strong> (outside Development): errors go to <code>/Error</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Header clean-up</strong>: removes <code>Server</code> and <code>X-Powered-By</code>; adds <code>Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>HTTPS redirection</strong> and <strong>Serilog request logging</strong> (one log line per request).</li>
    <li><strong>Static files</strong> from <code>wwwroot</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Routing</strong>, then the <strong>culture</strong> step: a <code>?culture=</code> query sets the language cookie for a month; then request localisation.</li>
    <li><strong>Session</strong> (30-minute idle timeout, in memory).</li>
    <li><strong>Authentication</strong> (Identity cookie) and <strong>authorisation</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>ELMAH</strong> error capture.</li>
    <li><strong>File-type blocker</strong>: any remaining request whose path has an extension other than common web assets (<code>.css .js .png .jpg .jpeg .gif .svg</code> and fonts) gets <em>403 Access to file downloads is forbidden</em>, apart from <code>/dist</code> and support zips.</li>
    <li><strong>Antiforgery check</strong> on every POST/PUT/DELETE except the login, register, logout and external-login pages, <code>/dist</code> and <code>/api</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Hangfire dashboard</strong> at <code>/hangfire</code> (Basic auth).</li>
    <li><strong>Endpoints</strong>: MVC controllers, Razor Pages, and the SignalR hub <code>/logsHub</code>.</li>
</ol>

